                <pb facs="0766" n="758" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg758"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/9007: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Valencia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wallner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Valencia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-03-06T13:00:00-04:30">March 6, 1939—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. A crisis probably precipitated by the unsuccessful communist attempt to seize
                    the Republican Navy in Cartagena has forced Negrin <pb facs="0767" n="759"
                        xml:id="pg759"/> and his Ministers to leave Spain. Power is now in the hands
                    of a Council of National Defense headed by General Casado, Commander of the
                    central army, and including Besteiro and other moderates which is expected to
                    follow the realistic policy. Public reaction favorable and order prevails here
                    and in Madrid.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wallner</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
